# FluxPhy UI/UX Overhaul Implementation Plan

A comprehensive enhancement of FluxPhy's Terminal User Interface to achieve a sophisticated "Cyberpunk/Retro-futuristic Hard Science Dashboard" aesthetic with functional bug fixes.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Scope Clarification**: This is a substantial UI/UX overhaul. The plan prioritizes:
> 1. **Bug fixes first** (Pause, Flux Rate, File Size, Notifications)
> 2. **Aesthetic changes** (Color palette, borders, typography)
> 3. **Advanced visualizations** (Oscilloscope, gauges, heatmaps)
>
> Some advanced visualizations (vector field heatmaps, analog gauges) are complex to implement in a TUI. I'll provide fallback simpler alternatives if needed.

> [!WARNING]
> **Font Dependency**: Monospaced fonts (JetBrains Mono, Fira Code) are terminal-dependent. The TUI will work with any monospace font, but Braille rendering quality varies by terminal.

---

## Proposed Changes

### Bug Fixes Component

#### [MODIFY] [main.rs](file:///Users/soheilsanati/Downloads/fluxphy/src/main.rs)
- **Fix Pause Functionality**: Currently, pressing 'P' only sets `state.paused = true` but doesn't pause the actual transfer. Add a `paused: Arc<AtomicBool>` shared between TUI and transfer task, with the copy loop checking this flag and sleeping while paused.
- **File Size Display**: The TUI correctly uses `state.total_size`, but verify that the initial size calculation matches actual file metadata.

#### [MODIFY] [flux.rs](file:///Users/soheilsanati/Downloads/fluxphy/src/flux.rs)
- Add pause support: Accept an `Arc<AtomicBool>` for pause state
- Check pause flag in copy loop and sleep while paused
- Ensure [calculate_total_size](file:///Users/soheilsanati/Downloads/fluxphy/src/flux.rs#127-152) returns accurate metadata size

---

### Aesthetic Overhaul Component

#### [MODIFY] [display.rs](file:///Users/soheilsanati/Downloads/fluxphy/src/ui/display.rs)
- **Color Palette Update**:
  - Background: Use terminal default (black)
  - Primary: `Color::Cyan` (#00FFFF)
  - Accents: `Color::Green` for neon green, `Color::Magenta`, `Color::Yellow` (amber)
  - Borders: `Color::Cyan` dimmed for inactive, bright for active
- **Border Styles**:
  - Active panels: `Borders::ALL` with double-line Unicode (╔╗╚╝)
  - Inactive panels: Single-line or dashed borders
- **Header Enhancement**: Add current date/time display
- **Footer Enhancement**: Dedicated keybindings row with proper styling

